  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GenDev - buy-in ITR - Women in the Digital Economy Fund (WiDEF) (GSMA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Bureau for Inclusive Growth, Partnerships, and Innovation (IPI)):  The Women in the Digital Economy Fund (WiDEF) is a joint effort between USAID and the Bill &amp; Melinda Gates Foundation to accelerate progress on closing the gender digital divide.  As part of the $50 million 3-year commitment of Gender Equity and Equality Action (GEEA) fund resources, GenDev&apos;s FY24 funds will be used to accelerate progress to close the gender digital divide by scaling evidence-based, proven solutions, including women-led solutions that improve women&apos;s livelihoods, economic security, and resilience. USAID funding will support programs that strengthen digital access and affordability; increase the design and development, especially women-led development, of relevant products and tools; increase digital literacy and skills training; address online safety and security; and increase sex-disaggregated data and research. This approach has been determined to best achieve the activity&apos;s theory of change, which is for WiDEF to: 1) help public, private sector, and civil society stakeholders to become better aware of the complex set of root causes of gender-digital inequities; 2) USAID, in collaboration with its partners, learn about the evidence-based solutions to address these inequalities; 3) for USAID and its partners to provide direct and aligned funding to to local entities to enable them to scale up these proven solutions; and 4) for the cohesive longer term impact of USAID&apos;s and its direct and aligned partners&apos; activities to accelerate progress to close the gender digital divide, thereby improving women&apos;s livelihoods, economic security, and resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
